#
# Witness, the audit log: a record of what changed through zxvd, which
# crossings it refused and held, which AI actions ran and what failed,
# gathered from zxvd's journal (journal.query, kept across restarts) or,
# with no journal, from its recent events (log.tail), stamped with zxvd's
# clock (sys.info). Witness links every entry to the one before it and
# checks that chain itself, asks zxvd to recompute the journal's hash
# chain (journal.verify), and joins the two witnesses (lpres_kjoin): a
# disagreement is held, never resolved by picking one. Read only.
#
# 7 later layers lean on this one, so its entries are general and owned
# here (CONCEPTS.tsv): one link of any chain of indexes, a count of one
# kind in any vector of kinds, and an audit record's fit. Nothing earlier
# fits: the inner blocks are capacities, shares, days from seconds and
# gcds; Murmuration's swarm shares (layer 61) weigh agents' tokens in a
# cycle, not a record's entries; Coffer and Seedbank, which the task names,
# are not built yet.
#
# zxvd's events carry no actor and no signature of their own, and zxvd has
# no method to append a signed audit entry or to say who approved a
# change, so Witness records what zxvd logged and seals it with the
# journal's hash chain; nothing is invented.
zxapp 1
id     witness
name   Witness
version 1.0.0
slot   18
layer  L1
matrix 18
icon   icons/l1/018-witness.svg
budget 233
needs  journal
needs  sys.read
model  apps/witness_model.c

# One link of the chain: an entry's prev index equals the index of the
# entry before it (last; 0 for the first) and its own index is past it.
# Critical (it says whether the record is whole), so witnessed over integer
# vectors: KRON and Sutra. Sutra holds an index to 9(18) and refuses a
# negative one; KRON answers: held.
provides chain_ok truth seq prev last
logic    kron  chain_ok apps/blocks/witness/chain.kron
logic    sutra chain_ok apps/blocks/witness/chain.sutra

# How many entries are of one kind (one want for the whole vector):
# critical (the counts shown), so KRON and Trebago, exact.
provides kind_count num kind want
logic    kron    kind_count apps/blocks/witness/count.kron
logic    trebago kind_count apps/blocks/witness/count.tb

# An entry fits its record: index, prev, kind and stamp, in MYRA.
provides audit_ok truth seq prev kind stamp
logic    myra audit_ok apps/blocks/witness/entry.myra

# Its own proof (zxapp.h K1): each entry at its edges, and where its languages disagree
check chain_ok seq=1,5,5,9,9,5,999999999999999999 prev=0,1,4,5,5,5,1 last=0,1,5,5,9,5,1 = true,true,false,true,false,false,true
check chain_ok seq=2,-1 prev=1,1 last=1,1 = both
check kind_count kind=1,2,2,5,3 want=2 = 2
check kind_count kind=1,2 want=1,1 = both
check audit_ok seq=1,999999999999999999,1000000000000000000,-5 prev=0,999999999999999998,0,0 kind=1,5,1,9 stamp=1700000000000,999999999999999,0,1000000000000000 = true,true,false,false
